(text "Pin names copied from the official v2 pinout image\n  https://nicekeyboards.com/docs/nice-nano/pinout-schematic\n  fetched 2026-11-05 (file pinout-v2.png on that page).\nPin numbers 1-26 are ours (the image has none): left column 1-13 top to bottom\n(USB-C end at the top), right column 14-26 bottom to top (BATTERY+ top = 26, 25).\nArduino labels on the image: D1=P0.06 D0=P0.08 D2=P0.17 D3=P0.20 D4=P0.22 D5=P0.24\nD6=P1.00 D7=P0.11 D8=P1.04 D9=P1.06 | D21=P0.31 D20=P0.29 D19=P0.02 D18=P1.15\nD15=P1.13 D14=P1.11 D16=P0.10 D10=P0.09.\nImage legend: when P0.13 is set low, power to the 3.3V pin is cut off (external VCC cutoff).\nImage note: bridging the BOOST jumper raises the charge rate from 100 mA to 500 mA." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 40.000 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7f5cf758-66a4-59fa-96c5-c7d169ad0b0e"))
(embedded_fonts no)
)
